title Actual runtime Skill admission - internal prerequisite
hide footbox
autonumber
participant "Skill application\n(future caller)" as Caller
participant "RuntimeSessionEngineRegistry\n(existing singleton)" as Registry
participant "AgentSessionFactory\n(existing singleton)" as Factory
participant "AgentRuntimeManager\n(existing singleton)" as Manager
participant "SkillCommandAdmission\n(application adapter, per invocation)" as Admission
Caller -> Registry : register(..., admission)
Registry -> Registry : acquire existing capacity
Registry -> Factory : create(request with runtimeValidator)
Factory -> Manager : prepare(agentId)
Manager --> Factory : actual PreparedAgentRuntime
Factory -> Admission : accept(actual runtime)
Admission -> Admission : verify identity, enabled, exact binding
alt admission rejected
  Admission --> Factory : RuntimeApiException
  Factory --> Registry : RuntimeApiException
  Registry -> Registry : release capacity; no Holder registered
  Registry --> Caller : stable error
else admission accepted
  Admission --> Factory : accepted
  Factory -> Factory : resolve model; assemble tools and Agent
  Factory --> Registry : ManagedAgentSession
  Registry -> Registry : restore messages; register Holder
  Registry --> Caller : active Holder
end
note over Caller, Admission
No Skill HTTP or submitSkill entry point in this slice.
No body expansion, history type, private snapshot, or version lease.
Existing ordinary callers retain the no-op validator.
end note
@enduml
